          "summary": "A Tennessee state legislative district will have no candidates on the ballot in November, ensuring whoever wins will have to carry out a write-in campaign — and it's unclear who that might be. G.A. Hardaway, the Democratic lawmaker who had previously represented the district, died in April. But even if he had lived, it was eventually determined that he didn't submit enough ballot signatures to qualify for the August primary, coming up just one short of the required 25. According to The Commercial Appeal,…",
